# Another shard root's re-created incarnation initialises without seeding its
# floor plus one: it keeps the generation it cached, the purged incarnation's,
# which the purge or its own catch-up has already covered with the floor. Its
# generation is at or below its floor, so the WAL refuses every claim it makes.
# The re-creation must start above the floor on every initialisation path.
MODULE: LiveGenerationAboveFloorSecondInitiatorKeepsGeneration
TARGET: LiveGenerationAboveFloor
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: another shard root's first initialisation keeps its cached generation
PERTURBS: S2Init

--- FIND
        /\ gen' = [gen EXCEPT !["s2"] = rf2 + 1]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the cached generation is kept.
        /\ gen' = gen
--- END
